== arm p7: prefix vs its causal twin (lower is better)
  twin, causal          0.4676   <- baseline, an existing 500-step run
  arm,  prefix p7      0.4673   delta -0.0003   <- THE EXPERIMENT
  arm,  causal          0.4666   delta -0.0010   <- mismatch control
  If the mismatch cell is far larger than the matched delta, the number is the mask mismatch and not the intervention -- Stage A's failure mode.
  the causal 2x2's LtSl cell read 0.4676 on the same 164 tasks (runs/n7c_2x2, same run family)

== paired, against the twin
  matched (prefix): delta +0.0003 (twin minus cell, so cell BETTER than twin)  SE 0.0003  z +1.1  n 164
    pre-registered rule: |delta| 0.0003 vs 2*SE 0.0006 -> INSIDE 2 SE, a null
  mismatch (causal): delta +0.0010 (twin minus cell, so cell BETTER than twin)  SE 0.0002  z +4.0  n 164
    pre-registered rule: |delta| 0.0010 vs 2*SE 0.0005 -> PASSES the 2-SE bar

== per-item count (separate measurement, not from paired_se)
  matched (prefix): 73/164 items worse than the twin
  mismatch (causal): 67/164 items worse than the twin
  The rule needs the item count to AGREE with the paired delta's direction: a mean that improves while most items get worse is a few large items, not the intervention.
